    <footnotes>
        <footnote id="F1">The reporting person, jointly with Haleh Abivardi, owns the Ordinary Shares as tenants in common. All of these shares are deemed to be beneficially owned by the reporting person. Pursuant to a reclassification exempt under Rule 16b-7, each Ordinary Share held by the reporting person will be reclassified into one Class A Ordinary Share (the &quot;Reclassification&quot;). No adjustments were made to the number of shares held by the reporting person.</footnote>
        <footnote id="F2">The reporting person, jointly with Haleh Abivardi, owns the Class A Preferred Shares as tenants in common. All of these shares are deemed to be beneficially owned by the reporting person. Each Class A Preferred Share is convertible into one Class A Ordinary Share on a one-for-one basis and has no expiration date.</footnote>
        <footnote id="F3">Pursuant to the Reclassification, each Class A Preferred Share was reclassified into one Class A Ordinary Share. No adjustments were made to the number of shares held by the reporting person.</footnote>
        <footnote id="F4">The reporting person, and, jointly with Haleh Abivardi, has controlling voting and dispositive power with regard to the shares held by vVardis Investment Holding AG. The reporting person disclaims beneficial ownership of such securities for purposes of Section 16, except to the extent of her pecuniary interest therein, if any, and this report shall not be deemed an admission that such shares are beneficially owned by her for Section 16 or any other purpose.</footnote>
        <footnote id="F5">Immediately after the Reclassification, 14,388,879 Class A Ordinary Shares held indirectly by the reporting person will be exchanged for 143,888,790 Class B Ordinary Shares.</footnote>
        <footnote id="F6">Each Class B Ordinary Share is convertible into a Class A Ordinary Share on a ten-for-one basis upon consent of the concerned Class B shareholder(s), the approval of the general meeting of shareholders and a corresponding amendment of the articles of association.</footnote>
        <footnote id="F7">Represents 50,000 Class A Ordinary Shares underlying restricted stock units (&quot;RSUs&quot;). The reporting person, jointly with Haleh Abivardi, owns the RSUs as tenants in common. All of these RSUs are deemed to be beneficially owned by the reporting person. RSUs were granted and fully vested on the date hereof. Each RSU represents a contingent right to receive one Class A Ordinary Share and has no expiration date.</footnote>
    </footnotes>

